["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0cae6-7e88-710c-8913-d70d29cb7b4c","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIGddd53b99f61f7cf3231d28c703a374b2be016078061ec70f17089487a65117a1","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/one-cli-verb-surface","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":4,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# Story: The verbs answer across members, and a refusal says which member refused\n\n## Outcome\n\nAn operator gets one answer for the whole workspace, and when something is wrong they are told\n*which repository* it is wrong in — rather than having to reproduce the refusal by hand in each one.\n\n## Context\n\nThe assembly is only worth building if the verbs use it. The requirement that makes the difference\nbetween a usable command and a frustrating one is attribution on refusals and on partial results.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n`protocol workspace list` (filterable by `--kind`, `--status`, `--member`), `crossings`, `show` and\n`members` all answer over the assembled graph, in text and JSON; every refusal names the member that\nrefused; **`members` exits `0` with an unresolved member listed as unresolved**, because a command\nthat failed because a colleague's repository is missing from your disk is a command nobody could\nuse; and a member that failed to load is reported with its failures rather than skipped.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nAny write verb across members, and `board`/`graph` rendering over the assembly — `list`,\n`crossings`, `show` and `members` are the surface this story delivers.\n\n## Open Questions\n\nWhether `board` should render across members is open; it is a rendering decision, and nobody has\nasked for it yet.\n","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:one-cli-many-repositories"},{"depends_on":"story:cross-repo-relations"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"list, board, graph and validate over the assembled graph. A refusal that does not name the member is a refusal somebody has to go and reproduce by hand.","title":"The verbs answer across members, and a refusal says which member refused"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIGddd53b99f61f7cf3231d28c703a374b2be016078061ec70f17089487a65117a1","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":4,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIGddd53b99f61f7cf3231d28c703a374b2be016078061ec70f17089487a65117a1"]}]